# Release: MANDATORY checks (all must pass)

Before merging to `main` or creating a release (tag and `make release`), run **`make release-check`**. It runs (in order):

1. **`make lint`** — gofmt -s, **go vet ./...**, and gocyclo -over 14. If formatting fails: `make lint-fix` then retry. If **go vet** or complexity fails: fix or refactor (functions stay ≤ 14).
2. **`make test`** — unit tests (`go test ./...`).
3. **`make cover-check`** — total statement coverage **≥ 80%** on library packages (`COVER_TEST_PKGS` in `GNUmakefile`; excludes `internal/cli`, which is covered by `cmd/pgwd` black-box tests). Requires Docker (starts Postgres via compose). Override gate: `COVERAGE_MIN=70`.
4. **`make test-integration`** — Postgres + Loki via Docker compose. Requires Docker.
5. **`make test-e2e-kube`** — kind cluster + Postgres + Loki + pgwd -kube-postgres -dry-run and pgwd -kube-loki -force-notification. Requires kind, kubectl, Docker.
6. **`make docker-scan`** — builds image, runs Grype with `--fail-on high` (override with **`GRYPE_FAIL_ON`**). Requires Docker; uses **Grype on PATH** if installed, otherwise the **anchore/grype** container via the Docker socket.

**These are NOT optional.** `make release` depends on `release-check`; if any step fails, the release is blocked.

**When VERSION changes** (same `chore/release-*` PR): (1) Regenerate `docs/demo.gif` with `make install && bash -c "vhs docs/demo.tape"` from repo root (`bash -c` so zsh does not break VHS). The demo shows `pgwd -version`. See `docs/README.md`. (2) Update `contrib/man/man1/pgwd.1` — `.TH` date and version. See `man-page-sync.mdc`. (3) **`make port-freebsd-sync`** and **`make port-openbsd-sync`** so this repo’s BSD port Makefiles match `VERSION`. Do **not** treat Bugzilla or ports@ as part of the release.

CI runs lint and tests. The Security workflow runs govulncheck and Grype on the image; both must pass (no `continue-on-error`). Do not push a release tag if CI or Security is red.

Releases are made only from the `main` branch.
